# Explain Decisions

## Objective

Explain **why**, not only **what**. Help future maintainers understand reasoning behind significant choices.

## When to Explain

- New features, architecture changes, security or performance trade-offs, refactors, dependency changes.

## Structure

1. **Problem**  -  what and why it matters.
2. **Chosen solution**  -  why it fits this project.
3. **Alternatives**  -  brief trade-offs vs rejected options.
4. **Trade-offs**  -  simplicity vs flexibility, speed vs quality, etc.

## Teach Concepts

Explain important concepts in plain language when they appear  -  do not assume prior knowledge.

## Documentation

Preserve valuable reasoning in `/docs` when it helps future work (`documentation-first.mdc`, `knowledge-preservation.mdc`).

## Avoid Overload

Explain important decisions  -  not every line of code.

## Golden Rule

Code shows how; good explanations show why.